title: Instructions/replace_in_tiddlers

Bulk find+replace across many tiddlers, with dry-run preview by default. Use for cross-reference renames, tag cleanups, or regex-driven rewrites.

|!Parameter |!Required |!Description |
|`rules` |yes |Array of `{pattern, replacement, regexp?, case_sensitive?, words?}` objects |
|`filter` |no |TW filter scope (default: `[all[tiddlers]!is[system]]`). Plugin tiddlers are never scanned, their shadow subtiddlers are |
|`include_system` |no |Convenience for `$:/` tiddlers; ignored if `filter` is set |
|`fields` |no |Field names to scan (default: `['text','caption','list','tags']`) |
|`dry_run` |no |Preview only; nothing written (default: `true`). Set `false` to apply. |
|`max_tiddlers` |no |Cap on modified tiddlers (default: 100) |
|`max_replacements_total` |no |Cap on total replacements (default: 1000) |

Each rule supports literal or regex pattern. Regex unlocks JS backrefs (`$1..$9`, `$&`, `$$`). Multiple rules apply sequentially per line.

When `dry_run` is `false` and the change touches more than one tiddler, a client that declares elicitation support is asked to confirm the resolved list of titles before anything is written.

For the full output format, dry-run preview shape, and array-field handling, see [[Bulk Tools]].

''Example prompts:''

* "Rename every `[[OldName]]` to `[[NewName]]` across the wiki, dry-run first"
* "Replace `\b(\w+)Widget\b` with `$1Component` using regex"
